> interested in hearing suggestions on how to improve this technique or
> alternately better ways to score early poison resistance.

Nothing you probably don't know, but...

MC3 protects well against killer bees' and others "the poison was
deadly", but not against the same from poisoned arrows and other
projectiles.

Poisonous corpses (killer bees, giant beetles/spiders, scorpions,
snakes, soldier ants, etc) are fairly safe once you have a unihorn or a
ring of sustain ability/PR or amulet of PR.

Learn which PR-conveying things are safe to eat without unihorn (or
extrinsic PR/sustain ability).  Cave spiders, quivering blobs,
shrieker, unicorn, black/golden/red naga or hatchling, guardian naga
hatchling (only!), centipedes, pudding, blue jelly, flesh golem, gray
ooze, pyrolisk, quasit, red mold, and some unique monsters.

Obviously some of those don't occur early, but cave spiders/quivering
blobs/shriekers/unicorns are common sources for me.  Red molds are
common early but the chances of PR are very low (still worth eating).

Wear uncursed unID'd amulets.

FINALLY, consider whether it's worth eating poisonous corpses even w/o
a unihorn.  I know mrivan does.  I'll usually hold off until I start
seeing mordor orcs--then I'll retreat and eat poisonous stuff if I have
to.



